b226dd71-89e3-53ba-931c-f7309d4db475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418439 #edb/ref 1080 "$$0.61$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418439 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418439 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb154b3d-66ec-5d69-b172-03533be8a6b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418440 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,001" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418440 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418440 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bb42c329-8069-528c-b75c-f226cec7f9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418424 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418449 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "35c53bd6-fdb5-5d5f-980b-becaa30267cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418426 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418430 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186418440 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186418432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418450 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "795337c1-be28-5aa3-ba9d-a058d2de96cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143439" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1071 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ drawn from a population with mean $\\mu =5$ and variance ${\\sigma }^{2}=4,$  determine the smallest sample size required so that the standard error of the mean is less than $0.02.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0c52d3d8-d8c0-58d1-b731-d5f1789535ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418454 #edb/ref 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}\n$$\n\nSince the population standard deviation is $\\sigma =\\sqrt{4}=2,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe require that the standard error is less than $0.02.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{n}} & <0.02 \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >\\frac{2}{0.02} \\\\ \\sqrt{n} & >100 \\\\ n & >{100}^{2} \\\\ n & >10\\,000.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest sample size is $n=10\\,001.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186418449 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143428" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1071 "A sample ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},{X}_{3},{X}_{4}$ of four bills is drawn from a population. The population has bills of two different denominations, $$5$ and $$10,$ distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Calculate the standard error of $\\overset{―}{X}.$ Round your answer to two decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de928809-8125-57ca-bec0-eb6d36dc320c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186418459 #edb/ref 1074 "If ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n}$ is a sample of size $n$ from a population with population mean $\\mu $ and population variance ${\\sigma }^{2},$ then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\mu ,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n},\n$$\n\nand the standard error is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]}=\\frac{\\sigma }{\\sqrt{n}}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the bills in the population have denominations $$5$ and $$10,$ and these are distributed in the ratio $3:2.$ Therefore, to compute the population's mean and variance, we can consider a population consisting of $3+2=5$ bills only with the following denominations:\n\n$$\n$5,\\,$5,\\,$5,\\,$10\\,$10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mu  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 10) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(15+20) \\\\  & =\\frac{35}{5} \\\\  & =$7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the population variance is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }^{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\sum }_{i}{x}_{i}^{2}-{\\mu }^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(3\\cdot {5}^{2}+2\\cdot {10}^{2})-{7}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(275)-49 \\\\  & =55-49 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the sample size is $n=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\frac{{\\sigma }^{2}}{n}=\\frac{6}{4}=1.5.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[\\overset{―}{X}]=\\sqrt{1.5}≈$1.22.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425729 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425756 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425729 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425757 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425729 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425729 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425729 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425760 #edb/ref 1